```js
// Hoisted like the pre-split `var pr`: assigned only after commitAndPush
// succeeds, and releaseLock() below must observe "undefined" until then.
var pr;
``

Hmm — wait, in the OLD code, `var pr = findStoryPR(scm, storyKey);` was INSIDE the try block, after commitAndPush. In the NEW code, `pr` is declared at the top of action (outside try) and assigned inside try. In the old code, `pr` was declared inside the try block — hoisting means `var pr` was hoisted to function scope anyway. So both old and new: `pr` is function-scoped via var hoisting; assignment happens only after commitAndPush succeeds. If an error occurred after pr assignment (e.g., in postThreadReplies), the catch calls releaseLock() but NOT releaseWipLock()... let me check the old catch:

Old catch:
```js
} catch (error) {
   console.error('❌ Error in storyTestAutomationRework:', error);
