```js
if (!prFound) return;
postThreadReplies(scm, prFound.number);
try { scm.addComment(...) } catch ...
``

Same — postThreadReplies outside try/catch; if it throws, it propagates to the outer catch (reworkErrorResult). Same as before. Good.

Wait — the rework discussion said a test "a failing SCM comment only warns — the rework still succeeds". That's about scm.addComment which is wrapped in try/catch. OK.

