Unlike the other extractions in this PR (which remove branches from `action()`), inlining this log back into `handleGitOutcome`'s `noNewCommit` branch would not change its cyclomatic complexity (CRAP stays 4 either way), so the helper isn't earning its CRAP keep — it's one more hop when reading the git-outcome dispatch.

Fine to keep if you prefer the named-branch symmetry with `createPrOrFail`; in that case a one-line doc comment (like the other step helpers have) would make the intent obvious.
